PCB PHOTOPLOTTER DEFINITION FILE
GERBER 6000 / 6200 WITH ABSOLUTE IMPERIAL COORDINATES IN 5.3 FORMAT

     PLOTTER DESCRIPTION
     ===================

MACHINE 	GERBER	6000/6200 emulator or controller described in this file

TYPE		PHOTOHEAD	      photo plotter output only

CODE		ASCII		      alternatives are ISO, EIA or EBCDIC

UNITS		IMPERIAL	      output is in 1/1000 inches

COORDINATES	ABSOLUTE	      alternative is INCREMENTAL coords

PRECEEDING	5		      Gerber coord format 5.3

SUCCEEDING	3

ZEROS		TRAILING	      include trailing zeros only

REPEATS 	INCLUDE 	      omit any repeated coordinates

GCOMMANDS	OMIT		      G commands not used by 6000 series

INITIALISE	OMIT		      no initialisation required for 6000

PARAMETER	37		      parameter block identifier  %

ENDBLOCK	42		      end of block character  *

CRLF		INCLUDE 	      add CR/LF to the disc file

TERMINATOR	M02		      end of program command for plotter

BAUD		9600		      baud rate for On Line Plotter only

STOPBITS	1		      also for on line plotting only

VARIABLE	NO		      fixed length magnetic tape blocks

BLOCKSIZE	256		      size of magnetic tape blocks

CROSS		NO		      no splitting of commands across blocks

FILL		0		      fill end of blocks with nulls

XLOW		0		      define table size for plotting

YLOW		0

XHIGH		30000

YHIGH		20000

SYMBOLS 	219		      number of apertures on the photohead


